+/* Image copies on a queue without a copy engine (the compute-only family)
+ * run as compute meta for every format, as the proprietary driver serves
+ * every transfer command on its compute queue with compute work on that
+ * queue's own channel (libnvidia-eglcore.so 615.78.08: a compute
+ * inline-to-memory parameter block and an inline-QMD kernel launch per
+ * command).  Depth/stencil aspects and YCbCr planes are copied through
+ * unsigned-integer views of the same element size (as panvk_meta.h does) and
+ * compressed formats through views of their block size.  The one layout
+ * that has no such view is pre-Blackwell D32_SFLOAT_S8_UINT, whose stencil
+ * shares 64-bit elements with depth: vk_meta needs each aspect's bits to fill
+ * whole components.
